                            <span>1. Kaiser’s Germany & World War 1 Effects</span>
                        </h3>
                        <span class="bg-blue-900/60 border border-blue-400/30 text-xs px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full">Topic 1</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="p-6 space-y-4 flex-grow text-sm">
                        <div>
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-brown-800 mb-2 flex items-center space-x-1.5">
                                <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-brown-600"></span>
                                <span>Kaiser's Aims & Factors</span>
                            </h4>
                            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-brown-900">
                                <li><strong>Make Germany a World Power:</strong> German economy was growing rapidly (produced a third of electrical goods), German population increased massively from 49 to 65 million, German people followed the army and supported financially supporting them. <em><strong>Difficulties:</strong></em> Arguing with the chancellor, hated the Reichstag – he claimed that “there is only one ruler… and I am he”, other European powers like Britain and France were more powerful, industrial workers were creating trade unions leading to 3 million workers in trade unions by 1914.</li>
                                <li><strong>Control the Political System:</strong> Prussia had a lot of influence and were heavily militaristic, Junkers (Prussian landowners) held a lot of power within politics and supported the building of an overseas empire.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div class="border-t border-beige-200 pt-3">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-brown-800 mb-2 flex items-center space-x-1.5">
                                <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-accent-burgundy"></span>
                                <span>Effects of World War I on the German People</span>
                            </h4>
                            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-brown-900">
                                <li><strong>Economy:</strong> The war had wrecked the economy so less money to spend on social issues eg unemployment benefits and pensions. Was only producing 2/3 of prewar levels meaning less money nad less tax revenue.</li>
                                <li><strong>Society:</strong> British navy blockaded the ports which led to food shortages. Wages were kept low while owners were earning bonuses.</li>
                                <li><strong>Political:</strong> Kaiser abdicated 9/11/1918 meaning there was a complete shift to a democracy.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div class="border-t border-beige-200 pt-3">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-brown-800 mb-2 flex items-center space-x-1.5">
                                <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-accent-burgundy"></span>
                                <span>Treaty of Versailles</span>
                            </h4>
                            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-brown-900">
                                <li><strong>Attitudes of the German people towards the Treaty of Versailles:</strong> The German people had been told that Germany was winning the war and Germany was never invaded so it came as a complete surprise when the armistice was signed. The government who signed it were named the "November Criminals" and the Treaty of Versailles was called a "stab in the back" and a "diktat".</li>
                            </ul>

                            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 text-xs mt-2">
                                <div class="bg-beige-100 p-2.5 rounded-xl border border-beige-200">
                                    <strong>Land:</strong> Lost 10% of land, 13% people, lots of natural resources (26% coal).
                                </div>
                                <div class="bg-beige-100 p-2.5 rounded-xl border border-beige-200">
                                    <strong>Army:</strong> 100,000 men, 6 battleships, no tanks, submarines and airforce, conscription banned.
                                </div>
                                <div class="bg-beige-100 p-2.5 rounded-xl border border-beige-200">
                                    <strong>Money:</strong> No fixed number at Treaty of Versailles, 1926 was fixed at 6.6bn.
                                </div>
                                <div class="bg-beige-100 p-2.5 rounded-xl border border-beige-200">
                                    <strong>Blame:</strong> War guilt clause.
                                </div>
