                    </div>
                    <div class="p-6 space-y-6 text-sm">
                        
                        <!-- First Instance of Weimar Culture 3 Boxes -->
                        <div class="space-y-3">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-brown-900 flex items-center space-x-2">
                                <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-accent-burgundy"></span>
                                <span>Stresemann's policies to fix Germany</span>
                            </h4>
                            
                            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs">
                                <div class="bg-beige-100 p-4 rounded-xl border border-beige-200 space-y-2">
                                    <strong class="text-brown-900 font-bold block">Economic policies</strong>
                                    <ul class="list-disc pl-4 space-y-1 text-brown-800">
                                        <li><strong>End of passive resistance -</strong> told the workers from the Ruhr to go back to work which meant they were making money again. </li>
                                        <li><strong>The Rentenmark created November 1923 - </strong>gave the currency value again and stopped hyperinflation. </li>
                                        <li><strong>The Dawes Plan 1924 -</strong> Negotiated a deal with the USA where Germany received an 800 million gold mark loan to kickstart its economy. It also lowered annual reparations payments and stretched out the payment schedule.</li>
                                        <li><strong>The Young Plan 1929 - </strong>Further reduced total reparations by roughly two-thirds and extended the timeline for final payment over 59 years.</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>

                                <div class="bg-beige-100 p-4 rounded-xl border border-beige-200 space-y-2">
                                    <strong class="text-brown-900 font-bold block">Foreign Policy</strong>
                                    <ul class="list-disc pl-4 space-y-1 text-brown-800">
                                        <li><strong>The Locarno Pact (1925):</strong> Signed with France, Belgium, Britain, and Italy. Germany officially accepted its western borders (giving up claims to Alsace-Lorraine), which massively reduced tensions with France and brought European security.</li>
                                        <li><strong>League of Nations Membership (1926):</strong>Germany was invited to join the League of Nations as a permanent member of the Council, effectively ending its status as a global outcast and restoring its "Great Power" status.</li>
                                        <li><strong>The Kellogg-Briand Pact (1928):</strong>Germany joined 61 other nations in signing an agreement renouncing war as an instrument of national policy.</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>

                                <div class="bg-beige-100 p-4 rounded-xl border border-beige-200 space-y-2">
                                    <strong class="text-brown-900 font-bold block">The Golden Twenties</strong>
                                    <ul class="list-disc pl-4 space-y-1 text-brown-800">
                                        <li><strong>Peace at Home:</strong>By stabilizing the currency and economy, extremist threats faded temporarily (including the failure of the Munich Putsch).</li>
                                        <li><strong>Foreign Investment</strong>American loans poured into Germany, funding public works projects like modern housing, schools, hospitals, and transit, which lowered unemployment and raised living standards.In general this was fantastic for German regeneration but meant they were dangerously reliant on American loans and this later led to the significant impact of the Wall Street Crash and the Depression. </li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Second Instance of Weimar Culture 3 Boxes -->
                        <div class="border-t border-beige-200 pt-5 space-y-3">
